            <div xml:id="d850">

                <pb facs="0751" n="739" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg739"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/517: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kelley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-29T12:00:00+03:00">October 29,
                            1942—noon</date>.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d850-f1"/>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1085. My 1052, October 22. The Minister of Foreign Affairs today, in response to
                    my inquiry with regard to the status of the negotiations for charter of Swedish
                    vessels to transport wheat from the United States, said that the matter had
                    practically fallen through as a result of difficulties arising out of the
                    agreement between the Swedes and the Germans that whenever a Swedish ship leaves
                    the Baltic another must replace it. He said that the Turkish Government was now
                    seeking to purchase two old Panamanian vessels.</p>
                <p>I raised this matter with the Minister for Foreign Affairs because the Swedish
                    Minister informed me yesterday that it was his understanding that the matter of
                    the charter of Swedish vessels had not yet fallen through. He said that he had
                    not yet received a definite answer from the Turkish Government. He also
                    mentioned the agreement existing with regard to the Swedish ships in the Baltic
                    but <pb facs="0752" n="740" xml:id="pg740"/> observed that there were Swedish
                    ships outside of the Baltic which might be chartered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kelley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
